    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d140">

                <pb facs="0175" n="167" xml:id="pg167"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.008 North Pacific/271: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-01-24T20:00:00-05:00">January 24, 1938—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>24. Your 51, January 24, 4 p.m., paragraph 1. The Department approves of your
                    leaving with the Minister for Foreign Affairs following your representations an
                    informal memorandum containing the text of Section 1 of the Department’s 20,
                    January 22, 3 p.m., and headed “orally presented” to be understood as for the
                    strictly confidential use of the Foreign Minister.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
